  <title id="bdl14scaleawaredropout-title">Scale-agnostic and scale-aware optimization of the injected dropout rate</title>
  <desc id="bdl14scaleawaredropout-desc">Left: the negative log-likelihood as a function of the dropout rate alone falls steeply from about 3.1 at a rate of 0.05 to a minimum of about 1.70 near a rate of 0.28, marked by a hollow star, and rises again to about 1.9 at 0.5. Right: a surface of the negative log-likelihood over the dropout rate and the base-10 logarithm of the scale factor S. A dashed curve on the surface traces the optimal scale factor for each dropout rate, falling from high scale factors at small rates to scale factors below 1 at large rates. A hollow star marks the best value on the slice with scale factor 1 and a filled star marks the lower global optimum at a smaller dropout rate on the dashed curve.</desc>
